{{also|yakka}}
==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|þakka}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*þankōną}}. Cognates include {{cog|fo|takka}}, [[w:Danish|Danish]] and [[w:Norwegian|Norwegian]] ''[[takke]]'', {{cog|sv|tacka}}, {{cog|en|thank}}, {{cog|nl|danken}} and {{cog|de|danken}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθahka/|lang=is}}
* {{audio|Is-þakka.ogg|Audio|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ahka|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-weak|þakkaði|þakkað}}

# to [[thank]]

====Conjugation====
{{is-conj-w4|þ|a|kk}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|þakka þér}} {{qualifier|singular}} (literally “(I) thank you”)
** {{l|is|þakka þér fyrir}} {{qualifier|singular}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka ykkur fyrir}} {{qualifier|plural}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)
* {{l|is|þakka yður}} {{qualifier|singular, formal; rare}} (literally “(I) thank you ...”)
** {{l|is|þakka yður fyrir}} {{qualifier|singular and plural, formal; rare}} (literally “thank you ''for'' ...”)

====Related terms====
* {{l|is|þökk||''a thank'', thanks}}

